@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core media. Set accepted same-server storage rather than retain backend placement as an open choice; preserve future separation only as later planning.
title MVP core file library — same-server private storage
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190
actor "Private library owner" as U
actor "Protected resume viewer" as V
node "Same Resumefolio server" {
 rectangle "Core Files / Operations\nMy Files & Media" as F
 database "Core private metadata / quota / protected references" as D
 folder "Private supported video / audio / images / text / docs\nOutside public directories" as B
 rectangle "Sharing admission\nCurrent link / publication selection" as A
 F --> D
 F --> B : type / size / quota validation
 A --> B : authorized direct / preview / byte-range bytes
}
U --> F : private upload / organize\noptional per-resume selection
V --> A : no owner login\nonly selected material
cloud "External YouTube link\nSimple externally hosted playback" as Y
F ..> Y : external link only; never private uploads
legend bottom
 Upload does not publish. No separate media platform/server/object-storage purchase.
 Protect consistent backups; destination and measured recovery remain engineering work.
endlegend
@enduml
